//! The contract face of the <%= module %> hexagon.
//!
//! # This is a shell, and the use case in it is a placeholder
//!
//! `keel add module <%= module %>` knows the context's *name* and
//! nothing about what it is for, so it cannot invent a use case.
//! [`<%= Module %>Command`] below is a stand-in with the right shape —
//! a command in, a result or a rejection out — and renaming it to your
//! first real use case is meant to be the first thing you do here.
//!
//! What is *not* a placeholder is the structure around it: the driving
//! port, the error type owned by this context, and the fact that
//! nothing in this crate names another bounded context.

